---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BriefingForm from '../../components/BriefingForm.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';




---

<BaseLayout title="Industries We Serve - Decoheron">
    <div class="container py-4">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="row mb-5">
            <div class="col-lg-9">
                <span class="badge bg-primary mb-3 px-3 py-2 text-uppercase fs-6">
                    Who We Work With
                </span>
                <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">
                    The Obligation Is Different. <br>
                    The Problem Is the Same.
                </h1>
                <p class="lead text-subtle fs-5 mb-3">
                    Every organisation we work with arrives with a different trigger. A licence condition. A new AUSTRAC obligation. A client's security schedule. A renewal questionnaire that asked a question nobody could answer honestly.
                </p>
                <p class="lead text-subtle fs-5 mb-0">
                    Underneath all of them sits one problem: the organisation has controls it believes are working, and no way to prove it. That is the problem we solve, and it does not change with your industry.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Industry Sectors -->
        <div class="mb-5">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary">Sectors We Work In</h2>
                <p class="text-secondary fw-medium">Find the regime that applies to your business.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4">
                <!-- Financial Services & Wealth -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Section 912A &middot; CPS 234 &middot; CPS 230</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Financial Services &amp; Wealth</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            AFS licensees, insurers, superannuation funds, and advice networks. Licence obligations to maintain adequate risk management systems and adequate technological resources, with APRA-regulated entities carrying CPS 234 and CPS 230 on top. This is the sector where the standard of adequacy has now been tested in court, which makes it the sector where the expectations are clearest.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Legal & Professional Services -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">AML/CTF Tranche 2</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Legal &amp; Professional Services</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Law firms, accounting practices, and conveyancers captured by AML/CTF Tranche 2 since July 2026, now required to hold seven years of customer identification and source of funds records. Firms already holding privileged client material, transaction data, and trust account details, with an obligation to protect it that has just become statutory rather than professional.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Healthcare & Aged Care -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">Privacy Act &middot; My Health Records</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Healthcare &amp; Aged Care</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Private hospital groups, specialist practices, diagnostic and pathology networks, dental groups, and aged care operators. Privacy Act obligations apply regardless of turnover, so the small business exemption offers no shelter. My Health Records adds a further layer with its own penalty regime, and health has been among the most-notified sectors since the breach scheme commenced.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Property & Real Estate -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">AML/CTF Tranche 2 &middot; Payment Fraud</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Property &amp; Real Estate</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Agencies, developers, and property groups captured by Tranche 2, handling identity documents and settlement funds through processes designed for speed rather than security. Invoice fraud and payment redirection remain the dominant loss mechanism in this sector, and both are email compromise problems before they are financial ones.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Critical Infrastructure & Adjacent -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">SOCI Act</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Critical Infrastructure &amp; Adjacent</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Organisations captured by SOCI, including many that have not realised it. Alongside energy, water, and transport, the Act reaches data storage and processing providers, healthcare, higher education, and food and grocery. Risk management programme obligations, mandatory incident reporting, and the prospect of direct government intervention follow.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Government Suppliers -->
                <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                    <div class="card bg-light h-100 p-4 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">ASD Essential Eight Flow-Down</span>
                        <h3 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Government Suppliers</h3>
                        <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                            Organisations that have already committed to an ASD Essential Eight baseline through a contract schedule and now need to meet it. The obligation here is contractual rather than regulatory, which makes it enforceable faster and with considerably less warning than a regulator would give you.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Everyone Else -->
        <div class="row justify-content-center mb-5">
            <div class="col-lg-10">
                <div class="card bg-light p-4 p-lg-5 rounded-3 border border-2 border-secondary shadow-lg">
                    <span class="text-secondary fw-bold text-uppercase fs-6 mb-2">No Regulator of Your Own</span>
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold text-primary mb-3">Everyone Else</h2>
                    <p class="mb-0 text-body fs-6">
                        If none of the above describes you, you are still subject to director duties under the Corporations Act, Privacy Act obligations above $3 million turnover, and mandatory ransomware payment reporting under the Cyber Security Act 2024. And your largest client's security schedule is coming regardless.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <CallToAction />
    </div>
    <BriefingForm hidden={true} />
</BaseLayout>
